# server/migrations/.no-down-allow-list
#
# Migrations on this list are intentionally shipped without a
# matching .down.sql. The CI gate at scripts/check-migration-down-pairs.sh
# skips them so a green pipeline is achievable without rewriting
# the history of every migration that landed before the policy
# took effect (P0-4, R03 / W1).
#
# Rules for adding a new entry:
#
#   1. Every new entry MUST be justified in the PR description
#      that adds it. "Foundational schema bootstrap, no
#      mechanical rollback possible" is the only accepted reason
#      for migrations newer than 100; for anything more recent
#      than that, write the .down.sql instead.
#
#   2. The entry is the migration stem WITHOUT the .sql suffix.
#      Comments use # at column 0. Blank lines are ignored.
#
#   3. The script complains if an entry no longer maps to a real
#      .sql file (stale rows are removed-but-someone-forgot-to-
#      clean-up bugs). Keep this file tracking current state.
#
# Cohort A — foundational schema (001-013). These migrations
# bootstrap the platform tables (users, accounts, agents,
# decisions, workflows, etc.). A mechanical .down.sql would have
# to DROP TABLE every base table in the right FK order, which is
# both a full schema rebuild and a guaranteed prod-data wipe.
# Rollback for these is "restore from backup", not "run the
# down". Documented in docs/RELEASE_QA_PLAYBOOK.md §rollback.
001_init
002_subscription_and_models
003_agent_scoped_model_configs
003_human_auth_bootstrap
004_multi_market_trading
005_admin_platform_settings
006_wallets
007_agent_marketplace
008_analysis_memory_layer
009_plan_action_watch
010_agent_ownership_inventory
011_decision_trace_snapshot
012_workflow_run_terminal_states
013_workflow_run_daily_uniqueness

